    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nDirectory buffers don't reload. I think a mechanism should exist for this - whether it be using vim._watch or via autoread & enabling checktime.\n\nrelated #41724 #41725\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nI see three ways forward:\n\n1. Do not respect `:checktime`, integrate with vim._watch with a provider API\n2. Integrate with `:checktime`, and couple the logic of respecting directory buffers into the autoread logic itself.\n3. Integrate with `:checktime` AND leverage `vim._watch` with autoread.\n\nI'm definitely partial to approach 3 - I think respecting `:checktime` is idiomatic. I also think that vim._watch is/will be a useful primitive for plugins to use (see examples in #41725). However, I lack context with autoread.",
    "closed_at": null,
